AGENTMESH — GETTING STARTED
===========================
Target network : Morph Hoodi Testnet
Chain ID       : 2910
RPC            : https://rpc-hoodi.morphl2.io
Explorer       : https://explorer-hoodi.morphl2.io

Prerequisites
-------------
  - Foundry  (forge, cast)   https://getfoundry.sh
  - Node.js 18+
  - pnpm
  - A wallet with Hoodi ETH for gas
    Faucet: https://morphl2.io/faucet  (select Hoodi testnet)


STEP 1 — Build the contracts
------------------------------
  cd packages/contracts
  forge build

Output ABIs land in packages/contracts/out/
The backend imports them from there — do not skip this step.


STEP 2 — Deploy MockUSDC on Morph Hoodi
-----------------------------------------
There is no real USDC on Hoodi testnet, so we deploy a mintable mock.
MINT_TO should be your wallet address (it will receive 10,000 test USDC).

  MINT_TO=<YOUR_WALLET_ADDRESS> \
  forge script script/DeployMockUSDC.s.sol \
    --rpc-url morph_hoodi \
    --private-key <YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY> \
    --broadcast

Copy the printed MockUSDC address.


STEP 3 — Deploy APIRegistry + X402Facilitator on Morph Hoodi
--------------------------------------------------------------
Use the MockUSDC address from step 2.
TREASURY_ADDRESS is the wallet that collects the 1% platform fee.

  USDC_ADDRESS=<MOCK_USDC_ADDRESS> \
  TREASURY_ADDRESS=<YOUR_WALLET_ADDRESS> \
  forge script script/Deploy.s.sol \
    --rpc-url morph_hoodi \
    --private-key <YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY> \
    --broadcast

Copy the printed APIRegistry and X402Facilitator addresses.
Verify on explorer: https://explorer-hoodi.morphl2.io


STEP 4 — Configure the backend .env
-------------------------------------
Edit apps/backend/.env:

  RPC_URL=https://rpc-hoodi.morphl2.io
  CHAIN_NAME=morph_hoodi
  GATEWAY_PRIVATE_KEY=<YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY>
  API_REGISTRY_ADDRESS=<APIREGISTRY_ADDRESS>
  X402_FACILITATOR_ADDRESS=<X402FACILITATOR_ADDRESS>
  USDC_ADDRESS=<MOCK_USDC_ADDRESS>
  PROVIDER_ADDRESS=<YOUR_WALLET_ADDRESS>
  TREASURY_ADDRESS=<YOUR_WALLET_ADDRESS>

GATEWAY_PRIVATE_KEY — the backend uses this to call facilitator.settle() on-chain
                      on behalf of the agent (no human approval loop).
PROVIDER_ADDRESS    — wallet that receives API payments (99% of each call).
TREASURY_ADDRESS    — wallet that receives the 1% platform fee.


STEP 5 — Install backend dependencies
---------------------------------------
  cd apps/backend
  pnpm install


STEP 6 — Start the backend
----------------------------
  pnpm dev

Server starts on http://localhost:3001

  GET  /                        health check
  GET  /registry/apis           list all on-chain APIs
  GET  /registry/api/:id        get single API by ID
  GET  /registry/provider/:addr get APIs by provider
  GET  /registry/stats          total API count
  GET  /payment/nonce           get a fresh nonce + deadline
  POST /payment/verify          pre-flight signature check
  GET  /payment/balance/:addr   USDC balance
  GET  /payment/status          payment layer health
  GET  /api/v1/btc              paid endpoint (0.001 USDC)


STEP 7 — Register a sample API on-chain
-----------------------------------------
  cast send <APIREGISTRY_ADDRESS> \
    "registerAPI(string,string,uint256)" \
    "BTC Price API" \
    "http://localhost:3001/api/v1/btc" \
    1000 \
    --private-key <YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY> \
    --rpc-url https://rpc-hoodi.morphl2.io

Verify it was registered:

  curl http://localhost:3001/registry/apis


STEP 8 — Approve USDC spending (agent wallet)
-----------------------------------------------
The agent wallet must approve the X402Facilitator to pull USDC.
This is a one-time on-chain transaction per agent wallet.

  cast send <MOCK_USDC_ADDRESS> \
    "approve(address,uint256)" \
    <X402FACILITATOR_ADDRESS> \
    115792089237316195423570985008687907853269984665640564039457584007913129639935 \
    --private-key <AGENT_PRIVATE_KEY> \
    --rpc-url https://rpc-hoodi.morphl2.io

(The large number is uint256 max — unlimited approval for testing.)


STEP 9 — Make a paid API call (automated test)
------------------------------------------------
A test script runs the full autonomous payment flow end-to-end.
Make sure the backend is running (step 6) and .env is filled in (step 4).

  node apps/backend/scripts/pay.mjs

The script does everything autonomously:
  1. Fetches a fresh nonce + deadline from GET /payment/nonce
  2. Signs the payment message with GATEWAY_PRIVATE_KEY (simulating an agent)
  3. Pre-flight verifies the signature via POST /payment/verify
  4. Calls GET /api/v1/btc with all x-payment-* headers
  5. Prints the HTTP status and BTC price response

On success the gateway settles the payment on Morph Hoodi via
X402Facilitator.settle(payer, provider, ...) — no human approval needed.
Check the tx on: https://explorer-hoodi.morphl2.io


How the autonomous payment flow works
---------------------------------------
  Agent                Gateway (backend)           Morph Hoodi
    │                        │                          │
    │── signs payment ──────▶│                          │
    │   (off-chain)          │                          │
    │                        │── verifyPayment()        │
    │                        │   (signature check)      │
    │◀── API response ───────│                          │
    │                        │── facilitator.settle() ─▶│
    │                        │   (payer, provider, sig) │
    │                        │                          │── verify sig == payer
    │                        │                          │── transferFrom(payer→provider)
    │                        │                          │── emit PaymentSettled
    │                        │◀── txHash ───────────────│

The agent only signs once. The gateway handles on-chain settlement.
The contract verifies the signature came from the declared payer address,
not from msg.sender — this is what enables gateway-mediated settlement.


Run contract tests
-------------------
  cd packages/contracts
  forge test -vv


Troubleshooting
---------------
  "RPC not available"
    → Check your internet connection and https://rpc-hoodi.morphl2.io status

  "Invalid signature" / "Signature does not match payer"
    → x-payment-payer must be the address whose private key signed the message
    → facilitatorAddress in the signing code must match X402_FACILITATOR_ADDRESS in .env

  "Nonce used"
    → Each nonce is single-use. Get a fresh one from GET /payment/nonce

  "Provider payment failed"
    → Agent wallet has not approved the facilitator (step 8)
    → Or agent wallet has insufficient MockUSDC balance
    → Mint more: cast send <USDC> "mint(address,uint256)" <ADDR> 10000000000 ...

  "Expired"
    → The deadline passed. Nonces from GET /payment/nonce expire in 5 minutes.

  ABIs not found (import error on startup)
    → Run forge build in packages/contracts first (step 1)
